    "body": "DUNCAN_NIGHT_REPORT_R01\nCYCLE_ID = DNR01-20260830-007\nSOURCE_WINDOW = 2026-08-30 / corrected machine-readable report after fail-closed parser rejection of comment 5466421791\nMAIN_HEAD_OBSERVED = b18ca6b9cce2dce6fe304ca8ae36c05df4f4dcb1\nDAY_EVENTS_REVIEWED = issue:204 current restore entrypoint; issue:206 Night School/Fortress terminal evidence; issue:198 Tier-1 silhouette law; issue:199 character drawing/value-band law; PR:111 DNR01-20260830-006 comment 5466262963; rejected DNR01-20260830-007 attempt comment 5466421791 and derived validation errors; Permanent Archive V1 head 6b3812b6eb097d42ab1dd033002f4fbc91909abe\nANIME_TOPICS_STUDIED = anime value grouping; three-value mass design; preservation of dark/mid/light semantic separation under exposure/gamma variation; avoiding value collapse and over-fragmentation\nOPEN_SOURCE_CODE_INSPECTED = OpenCV runtime 4.13.0; upstream opencv/opencv 4.x exact ref 755546643a671420fae0c20ec5d4cd24a228da8e; Apache-2.0; modules/core/src/kmeans.cpp k-means++ initialization/L2 assignment/center update; modules/core/test/test_math.cpp kmeans tests; cv2.kmeans KMEANS_PP_CENTERS; existing scripts/duncan_night_archive.py exact main parser contract reused for corrected durable syntax; no new framework/code\nREFERENCE_PRINCIPLES = issue #199 requires controlled 4-6 tone bands and macro-over-micro discipline. This bounded lesson tests a lower-order composition abstraction: preserve intended DARK/MID/LIGHT masses before adding final tone-band detail. Reference study transfers value-mass economy and hierarchy only, not copyrighted frames/designs.\nEXERCISES = deterministic synthetic anime-character value composition with semantic DARK/MID/LIGHT ground truth, macro lighting and mild noise; OpenCV kmeans K=2/K=3/K=6. Base: K2 macro-IoU 0.604609 and MID IoU 0; K3 macro-IoU 1.000000 centers 50.77/111.29/192.38 with one cluster per semantic mass; K6 macro-IoU 0.617559 fragmentation DARK/MID/LIGHT 2/1/3. Exposure/gamma case: K3 macro-IoU 1.000000 centers 65.38/134.39/222.38; K2 lost MID; K6 fragmented dark/light.\nVERIFICATION = fresh deterministic cv2 4.13.0 exercise. Base K3 accuracy/macro-IoU 1.000000/1.000000; exposure-shift 1.000000/1.000000; unseen-layout 1.000000/1.000000. K2 collapsed MID in all cases. K6 fragmented intended masses base/exposure/unseen.\nFAILURES = real Tier-1 black-fill transfer NOT PROVEN because no approved Tier-1 silhouette raster is discoverable through current public durable repository path. First report attempt comment 5466421791 was archived RAW but training_eligible=false because machine sections were not in parser syntax; validation errors OWNER_TASTE_MODEL_DELTA_MISSING, SELF_MODEL_DELTA_MISSING, SKILL_DELTA_MISSING. No code was changed; corrected report follows existing parser contract.\nROOT_CAUSES = two-value capacity collapses an intentional middle mass; excessive clusters can fit local shading/noise rather than composition. Parser failure root cause was report formatting mismatch, not archive failure: existing parser requires multiline section headers exactly `SKILL_DELTA =`, `SELF_MODEL_DELTA =`, `OWNER_TASTE_MODEL_DELTA =` followed by dash entries.\nREGRESSION_RESULTS = prior negative-space lesson replay: meaningful void areas base 4788/1799 px; moderate cleanup 4780/1799 px with foreground IoU 0.996977; aggressive cleanup removed both meaningful voids and dropped IoU to 0.748770.\nTRANSFER_TEST = changed/unseen asymmetric cloak/sleeve layout with exposure 0.94, gamma 1.08 and noise: K3 centers 38.46/96.56/179.05, accuracy 1.000000, macro-IoU 1.000000, fragmentation 1/1/1; K2 macro-IoU 0.530322 and lost MID; K6 macro-IoU 0.783587 with DARK/LIGHT fragmentation 2/3. Synthetic scope only.\nSKILL_DELTA =\n- value_grouping_qc: UNTESTED -> PARTIAL\n- negative_space_grouping_qc: PARTIAL -> PARTIAL\nSELF_MODEL_DELTA =\n- VALUE_MASS_CAPACITY_RULE = Choose the smallest palette capacity that preserves intended semantic value masses; fewer bands are not automatically cleaner when they collapse a required mass.\n- DETAIL_FRAGMENTATION_RULE = When coarse anime readability is the objective, extra value clusters are suspect until they prove structural benefit rather than merely fitting local shading or noise.\n- SYNTHETIC_CONFIDENCE_RULE = Perfect synthetic separation proves method behavior only; it does not prove production generalization.\nOWNER_TASTE_SIGNALS = issue #198 confirms identity/readability must survive detail removal and silhouette is primary; issue #199 orders BIG SHAPE -> SILHOUETTE -> PRIMARY CONTOUR -> STRUCTURAL INTERNAL LINES -> 4-6 CONTROLLED TONE BANDS -> sparse accents and rejects uncontrolled microdetail/noise. No new OWNER preference inferred.\nOWNER_TASTE_MODEL_DELTA =\n- VALUE_MASS_ECONOMY = CONFIRMED_SUPPORTING_SIGNAL only: existing OWNER laws support controlled palette/value bands and macro-over-micro readability; this is not a universal K=3 law and does not override the 4-6 production tone-band envelope.\nZORR_APPLICATION = Use DARK/MID/LIGHT as an early composition/QC abstraction before final 4-6 production tone bands. If focal hierarchy collapses at coarse mass level, adding rendering detail is not a valid fix; preserve semantic masses first, then expand controlled bands where form requires them.\nPRIME_CORE_CHANGED = NO\nPRODUCTION_MUTATION = NO\nCANON_MUTATION = NO\nMODEL_WEIGHT_MUTATION = NO\nNEXT_TARGETS = real approved Tier-1 non-mutating transfer when durable raster is available; inspect Krita/OpenToonz ready-made value/palette workflows; test 4-6 band expansion from preserved three-mass composition without identity or negative-space drift.",
